  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Tue May 12 2026\n\nWhile Friday's temperatures will still be near normal, we will climb \njust above. This is just the start of the first warm spell of the \nyear. Afternoon highs starting Saturday and lasting through at least \nthe first part of next week will climb into the low 90s for most and \nmid 80s on the Plateau. Definitely the warmest temperatures we've \nseen since last September.\n\nRain chances remain low -- for now. Models still aren't in great \nagreement, but there will be a low chance for a shower or a rumble \nof thunder late Friday night. Shouldn't amount to much. The good \nnews is that while the overall patterns are slightly different, rain \nchances should start to pick back up for Middle TN on Tuesday of \nnext week and could be with us for a few days. This would be in \nalignment with the current CPC 6-10 day outlook. Lots to work out \nbetween now and then, but things may be looking up for the mid-state \nin the rain department.",
